cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Make Me Unicorn in your research or product, please cite it as below."
title: "make-me-unicorn: A Deterministic Launch Gate for AI Coding Agents"
abstract: >-
  make-me-unicorn (MMU) is an open-source command-line tool that blocks AI coding
  agents from committing launch-blocking gaps: unverified webhooks, Supabase tables
  without row level security, secrets in the browser bundle or in git, and
  interpolated SQL. It runs as a hook in Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, Gemini CLI
  and git, is deterministic and offline, and also ships launch checklists for solo
  builders. Distributed as a Python CLI (`pip install make-me-unicorn`), a Claude
  Code plugin, and an MCP server.
type: software
